  "final_message": "I haven't removed `channel` yet, because something still reads it: `analytics-ingest`.\n\n- `analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34` reads `channel` from `OrderPlaced` with `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`.\n- `analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts:17` copies it into the `orders` table's `channel` column.\n- Its README (lines 27 and 31) lists `channel` as a required field. It says an event with a missing or unknown `channel` is rejected whole with a contract violation.\n- `analytics-ingest/test/ingest.test.ts:88` and `:158` test that rejection.\n\nIf I drop `channel` from the event, analytics-ingest would reject every `OrderPlaced` event once this is deployed. That repo is read-only here and owned by another team.\n\n`billing-service` is fine either way. Its test at `onOrderPlaced.test.ts:106` already handles an event with no `channel`.\n\nHow do you want to proceed?\n1. **Coordinate first.** Analytics makes `channel` optional or removes it, and then I remove it here. I can draft a note for them.\n2. **Remove it from the order model only.** The `OrderPlaced` event keeps `channel`, which means we'd have to source it elsewhere. That doesn't seem to match what you want.\n3. **Remove it from both now.** Do this if you know analytics has already moved off `channel` and I'm missing context.\n\nIf you pick 1 or 3, the change here covers these files:\n- `src/core/order.ts`\n- `src/core/events.ts`\n- `src/api/requestParsing.ts`\n- `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md` (the example call)\n- the tests and helpers\n\nIt also drops the `channel` validation and its test. One more effect: a request body that still sends `channel` would be accepted and ignored.",
